{
  "why": "The one surface <-> artifact-kind pairing rule (hub `app_opens_kind`, browser `surfaceOpensArtifactKindV1`): a plugin-level kind is opened only by the surfaces whose own dialect names it, even where a sibling app lists it as an input; any other kind is opened by the editor that declares it itself and by the viewers of that editor's exact dialect (kind, standard, subset); never a kind with another schema. `app` indexes `apps`, the descriptor's surface apps.",
  "liveDefects": [
    "Ticket 26/09/23 S15, measured inside `s` against hub 7800 on 2026-09-25: the browser admitted on the plugin-level list alone, so a note document (declaration-tree plugin, `manifest.artifactKinds = []`, `apps[0].artifactKinds = [s.note.note / note.document]`) downloaded and hashed its 14.9 MB component and was then refused with `The document component could not be verified`.",
    "Ticket 26/09/23 C13, measured inside `s` against hub 7800 on 2026-09-28: the hub issued a Spectator the block viewer (`s.block.block2d@1/*#viewer`, which declares no kinds of its own) while the browser twin still required the opening app to declare the kind, so the verified descriptor failed (`document execution target: descriptor mismatch`), the worker dropped the hub session and the viewer window showed `The document target changed. Reopen the document.` without ever mounting."
  ],
